# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# AIRA mobile — environment variables
#
# The Expo runtime reads `process.env.EXPO_PUBLIC_*` from the JS bundle, NOT
# from the device OS. Which file ships the value depends on WHO builds the
# bundle. Three layers, three audiences, three failure modes — set each layer
# correctly or expect silent breakage.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL
#
# Where the mobile app's fetch wrapper (apps/mobile/lib/api/client.ts) sends
# every /api/v1/* request. Falls back to http://localhost:3000 if unset, which
# means a phone on cellular gets "Network error" because localhost on the
# device is the device itself, not your dev server.
#
# Three places set this — each ships into a different bundle producer:
#
# 1. Expo Go (local dev with QR scan) → apps/mobile/.env.local      [gitignored]
#    Must be publicly reachable HTTPS — your phone can't hit localhost or LAN.
#    On Replit:   https://${REPLIT_DEV_DOMAIN}
#    Elsewhere:   ngrok / cloudflared / any HTTPS tunnel.
#
# 2. EAS native builds (TestFlight / Play / store)  → apps/mobile/eas.json
#    Baked into the .ipa / .aab at build time via the per-profile `env` block.
#    Source of truth for native binaries. See `preview` + `production` profiles.
#
# 3. EAS OTA updates (`eas update`)  → apps/mobile/.env.production.local
#    THE FOOT-GUN: `eas update` runs Metro LOCALLY to build the JS bundle.
#    Metro inlines .env* files using normal Next-style precedence
#    (.env.production.local > .env.local > .env). The `env` block in eas.json
#    does NOT apply to `eas update`, and `.easignore` does not protect either.
#    Without .env.production.local, your dev URL from .env.local leaks into
#    the production OTA bundle and silently breaks every TestFlight user
#    until you push another update. Mirror eas.json's production value here.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=https://airabynisarga.com

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Sanity checklist before shipping the first OTA update
#
#   1. `cat apps/mobile/.env.production.local` shows the prod URL (not
#      localhost, not a *.replit.dev domain).
#   2. `apps/mobile/eas.json` production.env.EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL matches.
#   3. After `eas update --branch production`, install via TestFlight and
#      confirm network requests hit prod (Charles Proxy or a logged request).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
